# iOS App Store Readiness (Expo / React Native)

Treat `my-mobile-app/` as the App Store product. Optimize for approval, privacy, stability, and HIG — not SwiftUI patterns that don’t apply here.

## App Store compliance

- Flag missing iOS permission strings before adding Camera, Photos, Location, Contacts, Tracking, Bluetooth, or Mic (`infoPlist` / Expo plugins). Never add sensitive APIs without a usage description.
- No private Apple APIs, no sideloading payment for digital goods — use StoreKit / `expo-iap` (or equivalent) if IAP is added.
- Keep Privacy Manifest / privacy nutrition labels accurate when adding SDKs that collect data (Supabase auth, analytics, push).
- Set `ITSAppUsesNonExemptEncryption` / export compliance correctly in `app.json` / EAS when shipping.
- Don’t deep-link around App Review (hidden admin-only features are fine if gated by account role, not by secret URLs meant to hide functionality from reviewers).

## Performance & stability

- Prefer pure functions and small presentational components; avoid unnecessary re-renders and heavy work on the JS thread during navigation.
- Use `async`/`await` with try/catch; never leave unhandled promise rejections in UI paths.
- Clean up subscriptions, intervals, and Supabase channels in `useEffect` returns.
- Keep lists virtualized for long data (`FlatList` / FlashList); don’t nest VirtualizedLists in ScrollViews.
- Crash-free bar: null-check session/profile/API payloads before render; show empty/error states instead of throwing.

## UI / HIG

- Support Dark Mode and system appearance (`userInterfaceStyle: automatic`).
- Tap targets ≥ 44×44 pt; don’t rely on tiny icons without hitSlop.
- Respect safe areas and the floating NativeTabs inset (`useBottomTabPadding`).
- Prefer system-readable Dynamic Type where text is content; don’t clip critical labels.
- Loading / empty / error states required for every network screen.

## Privacy

- Request permissions only when the feature is used, with clear purpose strings.
- Don’t log tokens, passwords, or PII to console in production builds.
- Avatar / media uploads must stay within documented moderation and storage flows.

## When changing code

- Explain *why* a change helps App Store approval, privacy, or stability.
- Prefer complete, shippable diffs for touched files — no half-wired permission plugins.
- Scope App Store work to `my-mobile-app/` and related Expo/EAS config unless a web API is required for the feature.
